-- title:
--   A local source-full bad-base estimate within one atom
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be finite and nonempty with decidable equality, $P$ an ordered coarse-fine complex, $e$ a positive ordered face, and $a$ an atom of an upper face partition. If $\alpha\ge0$ and $\beta>0$, the normalized density of the intersection of $a$ with its source-full atom bad-base support is at most $\alpha$ plus the mean of its immediate defect square divided by $\beta$.
